# Complete semantic translation of the historical standalone usbecm.wlcmd.
#
# The historical callbacks and entry points are automatic roots because their
# addresses escape through operation vectors, USB callbacks, or hotplug
# registration.  The seven bus_ops mappings cannot affect usbecm because its
# dev_ops has no bus_ops vector.
#
# OSLL produces identical analysis and function inventories with and without
# "one usbecm_state".  New locklint already distinguishes concrete object
# identities and needs no declaration for this focused module.
#
# The five usbecm_ds_ops target declarations historically pointed at
# warlock_dummy.  Current usbecm never assigns ecm_ds_ops, so this standalone
# comparison intentionally leaves those indirect calls unresolved rather than
# inventing concrete targets.
#
# OSLL groups the ecm_ctrl_if_no writes at lines 2466 and 2469 into one
# diagnostic, while native Sparse retains separate stores.  OSLL also retains
# a separate read for the compound assignment to ecm_init_flags at line 2338;
# Sparse reuses the value loaded by the preceding test at line 2334.  The
# runner checks those two multiplicities explicitly and compares all others
# exactly.
